# Brief constraints

This is the official TeamITG starter. Implement the test in the files it already has. Do not introduce a new app structure.

- All network logic lives in `src/api/index.js` (`getData`) and `src/api/helpers.js` (`request`). No other file may `fetch`.
- `VehicleList` reads data only through `useData`. Do not call `getData` from components.
- Native browser APIs over libraries: `fetch`, `<picture>`, native `<dialog>`. No CSS framework. No Redux. No new UI packages.
- ES6+, Airbnb eslint already in the repo. Keep formatting consistent with files you touch.
- Mobile-first SCSS with `min-width` media queries. BEM class names.
- Small Node 18 workarounds (`.npmrc` `legacy-peer-deps`, `NODE_OPTIONS=--openssl-legacy-provider` on start/build) are allowed. Do not upgrade webpack.
- Keep the original brief README. Add a short design-decisions section if needed; do not replace the brief.

```js
// ❌ BAD — fetch in a component
useEffect(() => { fetch('/api/vehicles.json'); }, []);

// ✅ GOOD — VehicleList only uses the hook
const [loading, error, vehicles] = useData();
```
